message: "If you use this project or its findings, please cite it as below."
title: "COLD READ: The Anonymity Half-Life Is a Property of the Reader"
authors:
  - family-names: "Syed"
    given-names: "Zaid Ali"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0003-4313-1510"
version: 1.1.0
date-released: 2026-09-27
url: "https://github.com/zaidwhy/coldread"
repository-code: "https://github.com/zaidwhy/coldread"
license: MIT
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.22309660"
abstract: >
  Measures how many words a person must write before a language model
  can infer who they are. Finds that the anonymity half-life is a
  property of the reader model, not the text - among three models of
  one size class, gender needs 50, 800 or 1600 words on the same text.
